 {"id":"fabro-0879","title":"gofib: add -pretty flag for aligned column output","status":"closed","type":"feature","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-22T19:50:57.960Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-22T20:51:51.893Z","description":"Extend the gofib CLI with a -pretty output mode.\n\nRequirements:\n- New bool flag 'pretty' via the flag package: 'gofib -pretty', 'gofib -pretty -n 10', and 'gofib -pretty -json' are all valid.\n- Pretty TEXT mode: two aligned columns, right-aligned index and value:\n    '   1:                    1'\n    '   2:                    1'\n    '  10:                   55'\n    ' 100:  354224848179261915075'\n  The index column width is the width of the largest index; the value column width is the width of the largest value. Both right-aligned, separated by ': '.\n- The largest index/value depend on n: for -n 5 the widths come from the 5th line, not the 100th.\n- Pretty JSON mode: JSON Lines, same objects as -json ({\"index\":<int>,\"fib\":\"<string>\"}); -pretty only affects text mode. Document this in the flag usage text.\n- -pretty with -n: both combine (pretty text for exactly n numbers).\n- Default output (no -pretty) unchanged: '<index>: <value>' with single spaces.\n- Extend fib_test.go: table-driven tests for run() covering pretty+n=5 (exact expected 5 lines including padding), pretty default (assert line count 100 and the exact last line), pretty+json (identical lines to -json for n=3). Compute expected strings in tests, do not hardcode F-values beyond small n.\n- No external dependencies. 'just qualitygate' must pass.\n\nDone when: 'go run . -pretty -n 5' prints the exact aligned 5-line block above (widths from the 5th line) and the gate is green.\n\nMerged from run 01M0NJZGX7BMJAJC3CZJZ0RNT0 (implementer + gate green; reviewer died on z.ai broken pipe, transient_infra — human override, output manually verified: -pretty -n 10/-n 12/default widths correct).","labels":["ready-for-agent"],"closedAt":"2026-08-22T20:51:51.722Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-8d26","title":"gofib: add -version flag","status":"closed","type":"feature","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-22T21:01:17.873Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-23T17:33:54.942Z","description":"Add a -version flag to the gofib CLI.\n\nRequirements:\n- New bool flag 'version' via the flag package: 'gofib -version'.\n- With -version, print exactly one line to stdout: 'gofib <semver>' with\n  semver taken from a package-level const Version = \"1.3.0\", then exit 0.\n- -version takes precedence over all output modes: 'gofib -version -pretty'\n  and 'gofib -version -json -n 5' also print only the version line.\n- Add a table-driven test covering run() or main-level behavior for\n  -version alone and -version combined with -json (assert the single\n  version line and exit 0).\n- No external dependencies. 'just qualitygate' must pass.\n\nDone when: 'go run . -version' prints 'gofib 1.3.0' and the gate is green.","labels":["ready-for-agent"],"closedAt":"2026-08-23T17:33:54.942Z"}
